<title>SWITZERLAND: Adecco with Q1 loss on goodwill charge.</title>
<headline>Adecco with Q1 loss on goodwill charge.</headline>
<dateline>LAUSANNE, Switzerland 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter of 1997 compared with first quarter 1996:</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net result	     68.7 loss	 vs 70.1 loss</p>
<p> Goodwill amortisation	114.0	     vs 103.1</p>
<p>Net profit before goodwill</p>
<p> amortisation		   45.3		vs 33.0</p>
<p> Operating profit	     74.0		vs 59.6</p>
<p> Sales			    2,334.7	   vs 1,806.3</p>
<p>Sales in regions:</p>
<p> France			   940		 vs 810</p>
<p> Rest of Europe		 594		 vs 433</p>
<p> North America		  609		 vs 434</p>
<p> Rest of world		  192		 vs 129</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name is Adecco SA. Adecco said in a statement that the 1996 figures were proforma as if the merger of Adia and Ecco had already taken place at the start of 1996.</p>
<p>The figures do not contain costs linked to the merger, non-recurring earnings from sold activities and earnings from activities not continued.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
